      "id": "CVE-2026-80921",
      "publishedDate": "2026-09-09T16:19:42.335Z",
      "lastModifiedDate": "2026-09-10T05:50:22.520Z",
      "description": "In the Linux kernel, the following vulnerability has been resolved:\n\nKVM: s390: vsie: zero stale crypto bits\n\nWhen shadowing crypto access bits from a format0 apcb (crycb 0 or 1),\nthe bits 64..255 are unchanged from whatever is in the vsie page in the\ncrycb and thus in the apcb. This gives a nested guest potential access\nto a device no longer available. Zero out the remaining bits.",
      "severity": 8.8,
      "fix_suggestion": "📦 受影响组件：Linux Linux\n🛠️ 修复建议：\n1. 确认受影响的版本范围（见上方 Affected Products）\n2. 升级到厂商官方发布的最稳定安全版本\n3. 检查官方安全公告获取补丁链接\n4. 如无法立即升级，实施临时缓解措施：\n   - 网络层：WAF 规则 / IPS 签名 / 零信任策略\n   - 主机层：最小化暴露面 / 禁用危险功能 / 输入过滤\n5. 修复后使用 NVD / 厂商 PoC 验证修复有效性",
